      "player": "Gem3P Stoic",
      "decision_index": 13,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "With the opponent tapped out and no pressure requiring interaction, this is the ideal time to cast Opt at end of turn or during the main phase to dig through the deck. While passing priority here isn't terrible (they could cast Opt on opponent's end step), they should at minimum cast Opt now or plan to cast it on the opponent's end step. However, the bigger missed opportunity is that Burst Lightning on Hired Claw while the opponent is tapped out would be clean removal of a threat that grows with +1/+1 counters and pings when Lizards attack. Removing it now prevents it from accumulating value, and the opponent can't protect it.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without casting anything, saving mana and cards.",
