    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem3P Stoic has 2 untapped lands and could cast Opt at instant speed during the opponent's end step, but more importantly, they're passing their main phase without casting anything when they have useful options. Casting Opt now to dig for a land drop (they need to develop their mana for Eddymurk Crab) would be reasonable, but the real issue is that they should hold up Spell Snare with their two mana since the opponent has a 2-mana-value creature already deployed and might cast another 2-cost spell. However, they could cast Opt at end of opponent's turn instead to hold up Spell Snare, which makes passing here defensible. The pass is actually reasonable if they plan to hold up Spell Snare and cast Opt at end of turn.",
